1. Primary owner requirement

The central reason for the installation changes is:

An approved installation operator who does not have root access must be able to perform a normal CLUE installation without entering or supplying a personal password.

Do not lose, weaken, bypass or reinterpret this requirement while repairing the current failures.

This does not mean every operating-system user may install CLUE.

It means an approved non-root initiator may install when the environment’s one-time prerequisites have already been provisioned.

The target environment NPID remains the owner and runtime identity of the installed application.

Keep these concepts separate:

Installation initiator != necessarily the runtime NPID
